IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wia-types`
IMPORT `wia-days`
IMPORT `wia-connection`
IMPORT `wia-disconnection`
IMPORT `wia-charges`

-- Water Industry Act 1991 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Seat: the water
-- customer.
--
--   "Must the water company connect me, by when; what interest is due on my
--    deposit; can the sewerage company still refuse my drain? Can my water
--    be cut off for non-payment, from when; can a limiting device be used?
--    When I move out, until when am I liable; can I insist on a meter,
--    revoke it, or be put on one against my will?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Water customer case` HAS
    `bank holidays`                                     IS A LIST OF DATE
    `the connection`                                    IS A MAYBE `Connection notice`
    `the deposit`                                       IS A MAYBE `Security deposit`
    `the sewer`                                         IS A MAYBE `Sewer notice`
    `the non-payment`                                   IS A MAYBE `Non-payment case`
    `the move`                                          IS A MAYBE `Moving out`
    `the s 62 notice`                                   IS A MAYBE `Section 62 notice`
    `the meter`                                         IS A MAYBE `Meter case`

DECLARE `Water customer position` HAS
    `duty to connect has arisen`                        IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day to connect`                               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `interest on my deposit`                            IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `last day to refuse my sewer connection`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `sewer refusal in time`                             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `premises protected from disconnection`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `earliest day my water can be cut off`              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `water may be cut off on the day`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `a limiting device would be an offence`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day I can be charged for after leaving`       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `I may require a meter`                             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the undertaker must meter me`                      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day to revoke my meter`                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the undertaker may impose a meter`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref ss 45-51, 61-63A, 106, 144-144B, Sch 4A
@export default The water customer's position under the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK): whether the duty to connect has arisen and the last day for the connection (ss 45-51), the interest on my deposit (s 48), and the last day the sewerage undertaker may refuse my drain (s 106); whether my premises are protected from disconnection (Sch 4A), the earliest day my water can be cut off for non-payment and whether it may be on the day (s 61), and whether a limiting device would be an offence (s 63A); the last day I can be charged for after leaving or after a s 62 notice (s 144), whether I may require a meter and whether the undertaker must provide it, the last day to revoke it (s 144A), and whether the undertaker may impose one (s 144B). Working days exclude the bank holidays given. Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Water customer case`  @desc The bank holidays, and any connection, deposit, sewer notice, non-payment, move, s 62 notice and meter facts
GIVETH A `Water customer position`
`the water customer position for` c MEANS
    `Water customer position` WITH
        `duty to connect has arisen`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`the duty to connect has arisen for` k)
        `last day to connect`                           IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN `the last day to connect for` k
        `interest on my deposit`                        IS
            CONSIDER c's `the deposit`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (`the interest on my deposit` d)
        `last day to refuse my sewer connection`        IS
            CONSIDER c's `the sewer`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the last day to refuse my sewer connection for` s)
        `sewer refusal in time`                         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the sewer`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the refusal was in time for` s)
        `premises protected from disconnection`         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` (n's `the premises`))
        `earliest day my water can be cut off`          IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` n
        `water may be cut off on the day`               IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`my water may be cut off on the day for` n)
        `a limiting device would be an offence`         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the non-payment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`a limiting device would be an offence for` (n's `the premises`))
        `last day I can be charged for after leaving`   IS
            CONSIDER c's `the move`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` m `, bank holidays` hols
        `last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` IS
            CONSIDER c's `the s 62 notice`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` s `, bank holidays` hols)
        `I may require a meter`                         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the meter`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`I may require a meter for` m)
        `the undertaker must meter me`                  IS
            CONSIDER c's `the meter`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`the undertaker must meter me for` m)
        `last day to revoke my meter`                   IS
            CONSIDER c's `the meter`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN `the last day to revoke my meter for` m
        `the undertaker may impose a meter`             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the meter`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`the undertaker may impose a meter for` m)
    WHERE
        hols MEANS c's `bank holidays`
